<title>FINLAND: EU TO BAN FINNISH TAX RELIEF ON XYLITOL -PAPER.</title>
<headline>EU TO BAN FINNISH TAX RELIEF ON XYLITOL -PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission will ban Finnish tax relief on xylitol, a sweetener made of birch trees, suspecting the relief constitutes hidden support to Finnish xylitol maker Xyrofin, business daily Kauppalehti reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The paper quoted an unnamed EU source.</p>
<p>Xyrofin is part of Finnish food, enzymes and sweetener group Cultor Oy .</p>
<p>Confectionery and packaging group Huhtamaki Oy has also benefitted from the tax reliefs granted for health reasons, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
